Every subset of 3 or more of the 10 points forms a convex polygon (since all points lie on a circle, no point lies inside the convex hull of others, and connecting a subset in circular order is convex). Thus the count is

$$\sum_{k=3}^{10}\binom{10}{k}=2^{10}-\binom{10}{0}-\binom{10}{1}-\binom{10}{2}=1024-1-10-45=968.$$

\boxed{968}

